{
  "id": "29265_fukidasu",
  "headword": "{噴|ふ}き{出|だ}す",
  "reading": "ふきだす",
  "romaji": "fukidasu",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (godan)",
  "gloss": "to gush out; to spurt out; to burst out laughing",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to gush out; to spurt out; to erupt",
      "explanation": "For a liquid, gas, steam, or the like to burst forth forcefully from an opening. Used for sweat, blood, water, lava, and similar."
    },
    {
      "sense_number": 2,
      "gloss": "to burst out laughing; to crack up",
      "explanation": "To suddenly and involuntarily start laughing, especially when trying to suppress it."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "29265_fukidasu_ex1",
      "japanese": "{温泉|おんせん}が{噴|ふ}き{出|だ}す。",
      "english": "Hot spring water gushes out.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29265_fukidasu_ex2",
      "japanese": "{火山|かざん}から{溶岩|ようがん}が{噴|ふ}き{出|だ}した。",
      "english": "Lava erupted from the volcano.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29265_fukidasu_ex3",
      "japanese": "パイプが{破裂|はれつ}して、{勢|いきお}いよく{水|みず}が{噴|ふ}き{出|だ}した。",
      "english": "The pipe burst and water spurted out with great force.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29265_fukidasu_ex4",
      "japanese": "{思|おも}わず{噴|ふ}き{出|だ}す。",
      "english": "I burst out laughing in spite of myself.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29265_fukidasu_ex5",
      "japanese": "{彼|かれ}の{真面目|まじめ}な{顔|かお}を{見|み}て、つい{噴|ふ}き{出|だ}してしまった。",
      "english": "Seeing his serious face, I couldn't help cracking up.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29265_fukidasu_ex6",
      "japanese": "{授業中|じゅぎょうちゅう}に{笑|わら}いをこらえきれず、{噴|ふ}き{出|だ}してしまった。",
      "english": "Unable to hold back my laughter during class, I burst out laughing.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        2
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: Used both ways ({自他|じた}). Most often intransitive — the substance is the subject ({水|みず}が{噴|ふ}き{出|だ}す) — but it can be transitive when something forces the substance out ({鯨|くじら}が{潮|しお}を{噴|ふ}き{出|だ}す). Compound of {噴|ふ}く (to spew) + {出|だ}す.\n\nUSAGE:\nSense 1 stresses a forceful, eruptive emergence. For the \"burst out laughing\" meaning, the spelling {吹|ふ}き{出|だ}す is also common.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {汗|あせ}が{噴|ふ}き{出|だ}す: for sweat to pour out\n- {勢|いきお}いよく{噴|ふ}き{出|だ}す: to gush out forcefully\n- {思|おも}わず{噴|ふ}き{出|だ}す: to burst out laughing involuntarily",
